"""Read-only final-state evaluator base for the macOS OpenNote saved-posts family.

Serves the three macOS OpenNote tasks whose per-task evaluator files carry only a
``TASK_PARAMS`` dict and delegate here via ``super().evaluate(merged)``:

    OpenNoteCoatSwapSavedEvaluator
    OpenNoteHarborCoffeeSavedEvaluator
    OpenNoteWeekendResetSavedEvaluator

Judgement surface
-----------------
The durable state is read from OpenNote's guest-loopback ``GET /api/evaluation``
and asserted check by check::

    session.logged_in, session.current_user
    post.<title>.{unique,body,category,location,tags,text_cover}    (x3 posts)
    source_note.{unique,comment,saved[,liked]}
    final_ui.{foreground_opennote,saved_view}

Notes on the observed shape:

* ``post.<title>.text_cover`` compares ``cover_prefix``, the first 48 characters
  of the cover value, and requires an accepted text cover to be a
  ``data:image/png;base64,`` URI whose PNG is 1200x1500.
* ``post.<title>.tags`` is compared as an *ordered* list, not a set.
* the app's port is discovered at run time (the recorded ``candidate_ports`` are
  stale) and the answering port is reported in ``state_diagnostics``.

Offline hook
------------
``evaluate`` also accepts a pre-collected evidence mapping at
``context["collected_state"]`` -- ``{"api_evaluation": <doc>, "port": <int>}`` --
and uses it instead of running a guest script, which makes the class testable
without a live runtime.
"""

